---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SupportEmail from '../../components/SupportEmail.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Keyboard Studio';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for Keyboard Studio. Learn how typing data, phrases, settings, Full Access, and local storage are handled.';
const effectiveDate = 'July 28, 2026';
const lastUpdated = 'July 28, 2026';
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Keyboard Studio Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how the developer of Keyboard Studio handles
        information in the Keyboard Studio App and Keyboard Extension for iPhone
        and iPad.
      </p>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span>Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</span>
        <span>Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow prose" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
      <p class="toc__title" id="toc-heading">On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#scope">Product scope</a></li>
        <li><a href="#collection">Developer collection practices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#local-storage">Local storage</a></li>
        <li><a href="#typed-text">Typed text</a></li>
        <li><a href="#document-context">Document context</a></li>
        <li><a href="#phrases">Quick Phrases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#dictionary">Personal Dictionary</a></li>
        <li><a href="#themes">Themes and preferences</a></li>
        <li><a href="#esdb">Bundled ESDB lexicon</a></li>
        <li><a href="#full-access">Full Access</a></li>
        <li><a href="#app-group">App Group synchronization</a></li>
        <li><a href="#click-audio">Keyboard click audio</a></li>
        <li><a href="#network">Network access</a></li>
        <li><a href="#analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sdks">Third-party SDKs</a></li>
        <li><a href="#accounts">Accounts and cloud services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
        <li><a href="#deletion">Data deletion</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="scope">Product scope</h2>
    <p>
      This policy applies to Keyboard Studio, including the containing App and the
      Keyboard Extension, for iPhone and iPad. It describes data practices of the
      developer of Keyboard Studio and the App itself. It does not describe every
      form of diagnostic or system data that Apple or the operating system may
      process independently of the developer.
    </p>

    <h2 id="collection">Developer collection practices</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Keyboard Studio does not collect, transmit, sell, or share typed text.
      </strong>
      The developer does not operate a backend service that receives keystrokes,
      document content, Quick Phrases, Personal Dictionary entries, or keyboard
      settings from Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="local-storage">Local storage</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Quick Phrases, Personal Dictionary entries, custom themes, and settings are
        stored locally.
      </strong>
      Data created or configured in Keyboard Studio remains on your device, subject
      to normal iOS storage behavior and optional local App Group sharing described
      below.
    </p>

    <h2 id="typed-text">Typed text</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio does not collect, transmit, sell, or share typed text. There
      is no feature that uploads keystrokes to the developer or to a remote service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="document-context">Document context</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Keyboard Studio does not transmit surrounding document context.</strong>
      The App and Keyboard Extension are not designed to send surrounding text from
      documents or input fields to a remote destination.
    </p>

    <h2 id="phrases">Quick Phrases</h2>
    <p>
      Quick Phrases you create are stored locally. When Full Access is enabled,
      phrases created in the containing App may be available to the Keyboard
      Extension through the local App Group container. Quick Phrases are not
      uploaded by Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="dictionary">Personal Dictionary</h2>
    <p>
      Personal Dictionary entries you create are stored locally. When Full Access
      is enabled, entries created in the containing App may be available to the
      Keyboard Extension through the local App Group container. Personal Dictionary
      data is not uploaded by Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="themes">Themes and preferences</h2>
    <p>
      Themes, layout choices, sound preferences, haptic preferences, and related
      settings are stored locally. With Full Access enabled, settings saved in the
      containing App may synchronize to the Keyboard Extension through the local
      App Group container.
    </p>

    <h2 id="esdb">Bundled ESDB lexicon</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        The built-in ESDB lexicon is bundled in the Keyboard Extension and operates
        offline.
      </strong>
      English Speller Database (ESDB), formerly SCOWL, is included for local
      lexicon features. Full license and attribution are available offline inside
      the Keyboard Studio App. Keyboard Studio does not claim ownership of ESDB.
    </p>

    <h2 id="full-access">Full Access</h2>
    <p>
      Full Access is optional. Without Full Access, basic typing, the bundled
      offline lexicon, gestures, layouts, and safe defaults remain available.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Full Access may allow the Keyboard Extension to read locally shared
        settings, Quick Phrases, and Personal Dictionary data from the App Group
        container and to request system keyboard click audio.
      </strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Full Access does not activate a network feature.</strong>
      Full Access does not enable networking in Keyboard Studio. Keyboard Studio
      contains no feature that uploads keystrokes.
    </p>

    <h2 id="app-group">App Group synchronization</h2>
    <p>
      When Full Access is enabled, settings, Quick Phrases, and Personal Dictionary
      data may synchronize between the containing App and the Keyboard Extension
      through a local App Group container on the device. This synchronization is
      local and is not a cloud synchronization service operated by Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="click-audio">Keyboard click audio</h2>
    <p>
      When Full Access is enabled and related settings are turned on, Keyboard
      Studio may request system keyboard click audio. Full Access is not limited to
      sound; it may also allow local reading of shared settings, Quick Phrases, and
      Personal Dictionary data as described above.
    </p>

    <h2 id="network">Network access</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio contains no network feature for uploading keystrokes,
      phrases, dictionary entries, themes, or settings. Full Access does not enable
      networking in Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio does not include analytics, tracking, or advertising for the
      purpose of collecting typed text or user behavior for the developer. There is
      no advertising in Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sdks">Third-party SDKs</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Keyboard Studio contains no analytics SDK, advertising SDK, account service,
        or cloud synchronization service.
      </strong>
    </p>

    <h2 id="accounts">Accounts and cloud services</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio does not provide an account system and does not operate a
      cloud synchronization service for keyboard data. Features described in this
      policy rely on local storage and, where enabled, local App Group sharing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio is a general-audience keyboard product. The developer does not
      knowingly collect personal information from children through Keyboard Studio,
      because the App is not designed to collect personal information from users.
    </p>

    <h2 id="deletion">Data deletion</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Deleting the App may remove locally stored App data and settings, subject to
        normal iOS behavior.
      </strong>
      Because Keyboard Studio does not maintain a developer-operated cloud copy of
      your phrases, dictionary entries, or settings, there is no separate remote
      deletion request process for that data.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. The Last Updated date
      at the top of this page will change when updates are published on this
      website. Continued use of Keyboard Studio after an update means you should
      review the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions about Keyboard Studio, contact the developer at
      <SupportEmail subject="Keyboard Studio Privacy" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page describes developer and App practices. It is not a certification of
      legal compliance and is not legal advice.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
